\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {12}{\ignorespaces Cross-family panel (EXP-H-full). LOO accuracy for the refusal-count rule (regex; extractor-independent) and the 5-feature LLM pipeline under three extractors: Claude Haiku, Mistral Large~3, and Llama~3.3~70B (two non-Anthropic cross-family extractors). Same equalized trials per target. $\dagger $: same-family cell. $\ddagger $: Qwen~2.5~32B produces zero refusal markers in both conditions under RLHF agreeableness smoothing (Section~\ref {sec:qwen_scale_sweep}), so the rule collapses to chance by construction; included for transparency. \textbf  {Refusal-count column uses per-target LOO (threshold optimized independently per target)}, so values differ from Table~\ref {tab:refusal_only} (pooled-LOO on 689 trials): the two tables correspond to different deployment regimes (per-target calibration here vs.\ shared threshold there), not different data. ``Avg CF gap'' is the per-target mean of (Haiku $-$ Mistral~L3) and (Haiku $-$ Llama~70B), in percentage points.}}{18}{table.caption.44}\protected@file@percent }
