\newlabel{tab:whitebox_probe}{{13}{19}{White-box LR probing baseline on equalized trials (EXP-P). LOO accuracy with Wilson 95\% CIs. Refusal-count column is from Table~\ref {tab:cross_family_panel}. Llama~3B uses \texttt {Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct}; Mistral~7B uses the \texttt {Mistral-7B-v0.1} base checkpoint (S2/V17: Instruct-checkpoint sweep requires separate extraction; the base-checkpoint sweep reuses V16 infrastructure and is reported as a preliminary per-layer panel). For both targets we sweep all layer positions $\times $ \{last-token, mean-pool\} and report the global best-layer per pooling strategy (Fig.~\ref {fig:probe_layer_curve})}{table.caption.46}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Per-layer $\times $ \{last-token, mean-pool\} LR probe LOO accuracy on equalized-transcript first responses ($n=100$ per target). \textbf  {(a)} Llama 3.2 3B Instruct: last-token peaks at layer 12 (67\%); mean-pool peaks at layer 13 (62\%); both collapse at deeper layers. \textbf  {(b)} Mistral 7B base checkpoint (S2/V17): both poolings peak at layer 4 (last-token 65\%, mean-pool 66\%) with mid-depth flat band around 55--60\% and decline at layers 24--32. Dashed horizontal line is the refusal-count rule (61\% Llama; 68\% Mistral); dotted line is chance. $^\dagger $Mistral sweep uses the base checkpoint; Instruct-checkpoint replication is future work.}}{20}{figure.caption.47}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:probe_layer_curve}{{3}{20}{Per-layer $\times $ \{last-token, mean-pool\} LR probe LOO accuracy on equalized-transcript first responses ($n=100$ per target). \textbf {(a)} Llama 3.2 3B Instruct: last-token peaks at layer 12 (67\%); mean-pool peaks at layer 13 (62\%); both collapse at deeper layers. \textbf {(b)} Mistral 7B base checkpoint (S2/V17): both poolings peak at layer 4 (last-token 65\%, mean-pool 66\%) with mid-depth flat band around 55--60\% and decline at layers 24--32. Dashed horizontal line is the refusal-count rule (61\% Llama; 68\% Mistral); dotted line is chance. $^\dagger $Mistral sweep uses the base checkpoint; Instruct-checkpoint replication is future work}{figure.caption.47}{}}
